{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
  "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "B. Eric Restuccia, Solicitor General (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RESTUCCIA: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In rejecting Mr. Thompkins's Miranda claim and ineffective assistance of counsel claim, the Michigan courts did not unreasonably apply clearly established Supreme Court precedent. I plan to focus on the Miranda claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But he didn't -- he didn't waive them. And quite unlike Butler -- Butler, if I have it right, said, \"I'll talk to you.\" So that was a statement --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell me without more detail, which is what the circuit court said, about what the limited responses -- I'm using your word -- were. How do we -- how can we imply waiver?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Wait. Do -- do we have any case that says that 2 and a quarter hours is too long?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Respondent's confession was properly admitted at his trial. I\u2019d like to go right to some of the questions that this Court had about the language that was used in the Miranda decision and in the Butler decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So are you going to go on -- because this is right where you are. Are you going to go on to say that, in the Miranda context, the failure to assert can -- can suffice to allow the questioning to proceed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you\u2019re saying there -- there\u2019s a difference, I -- I assume, between not waiving and positively asserting your right not to be interrogated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Of course, those facts are relevant only if we accept your -- your principal assertion, which is that you -- you don't have to invoke the right and interrogation must cease immediately. If we agree with that, then all of these facts become relevant. But if we think that, until you invoke the right, the police can continue to ask you questions and it's up to you to answer or not, then those facts are really not relevant at all, are they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell me when the police have to stop? They read somebody their rights; the person says nothing. Are you saying at that point they have to stop?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Then they have to stop?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Your argument would be the same if this was compressed to 45 minutes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So, in this case, after 2 hours and 15 minutes when he gave the answers I just said, when did he waive his Miranda rights?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask, can you go back to page 14 in your reply brief? \"Once warnings have been given, the subsequent procedure is clear. If the individual indicates in any manner, at any time prior to or during questioning, that he wishes to remain silent, the interrogation must cease.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: So the question is whether during those two hours by not answering a -- a number of questions, did he indicate in any way that he wished to remain silent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. RESTUCCIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RESTUCCIA: Well, what happens, though, in Davis, this Court made clear for the purpose of invocation, that the invocation has to be unambiguous because the police have to know when they have to cut off their questioning. The -- so, if it's ambiguous, it's ultimately, for the question of invocation, his burden to assert the right to take an affirmative action to show, I don't want to answer any questions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. RESTUCCIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Detective Helgert believed, through his limited responses, the give and take of part of this interview, that he was a willing participant in the interview."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a160f9b9dada48e601a574df9d00f904174bfc94375d39d6d805511332175f3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a160f9b9dada-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is the factual record that was established by the State courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1470",
      "confidence": 0.0,
